  "instruction": "Begin with /home/user/Desktop/simple_cam_job.step in FreeCAD 0.21.2 Path/CAM. Create one editable native Path/CAM Job containing active Face, Drilling, and Profile operations. T1 must be a native 10 mm end mill, tool number 1, used for Face and Profile at S7000 rpm and F700 mm/min horizontal cutting feed. T2 must be a native 5 mm drill, tool number 2, used for Drilling at S5000 rpm and F180 mm/min vertical cutting feed. Choose safe, physically reasonable stock, setup, origin, operation geometry, depths, and clearances for the supplied block; drilling locations and quantity are your choice, but at least one location must actually enter the material. Use the native linuxcnc or grbl postprocessor. Save the editable Job and matching posted G-code/NC output using exactly these absolute file paths: /home/user/Desktop/task-6.FCStd and /home/user/Desktop/task-6.nc. [Software] To use FreeCAD, run `freecad` from a terminal (use the full executable path if it is not on PATH). Open the part in FreeCAD from `/usr/bin/freecad`, then carry out the Path workbench edits when working on `simple_cam_job.step`.",
